1
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Michael Jackson's Thriller is a horror, thriller,
music film directed by John Landis.

2
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
A night at the movies turns terrifying when Michael
and his date are attacked by zombies.

3
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Released at the height of Thriller’s success, the short film redefined the music
video, broke racial barriers, and became the first inducted into the U.S.

4
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
National Film Registry.

5
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Michael Jackson, played by Michael Jackson.

6
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Michael's Girlfriend, played by Ola Ray.

7
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Narrator (voice), played by Vincent Price.

8
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Zombie (uncredited), played by Cynthia Garris.

9
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Zombie (uncredited), played by Mick Garris.

10
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Dancer (uncredited), played by Hanala Sagal.

11
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Michael Jackson's Thriller is the music video for the song "Thriller" by the
American singer Michael Jackson, released on December 2, 1983.

12
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,000
It was directed by John Landis, written by Jackson and
Landis, and stars Jackson and Ola Ray.

13
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:10,000
It references numerous horror films and has Jackson
dancing with a horde of zombies.

14
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Jackson's sixth album, Thriller, was released in November 1982 and spent months at the top of the
Billboard 200, backed by successful videos for the singles "Billie Jean" and "Beat It".

15
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
In July 1983, after Thriller was displaced from the top of the chart,
Jackson and his team decided to release "Thriller" as a single.

16
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Jackson hired Landis to direct the video after seeing his
1981 film An American Werewolf in London.

17
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:02,000
It was filmed at various locations in Los Angeles, including the Palace
Theater, with a budget much larger than previous music videos.

18
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:30,000
A making-of documentary, Making Michael Jackson's Thriller,
was produced to sell to television networks.

19
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Michael Jackson's Thriller was launched to great
anticipation and played regularly on MTV.

20
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:26,000
It doubled sales of Thriller, helping it become the best-selling album in history, and the
documentary sold over a million copies, becoming the best-selling VHS tape at the time.

21
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:54,000
It is credited for transforming music videos into a serious art form, breaking down racial barriers in popular
entertainment, popularizing the making-of documentary format, and driving home video sales.

22
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:22,000
The success made Jackson a dominant force in global pop culture.

23
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Many elements of Michael Jackson's Thriller have had a lasting impact on popular culture, such as the
zombie dance and Jackson's red jacket, designed by Landis's wife, Deborah Nadoolman.

24
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,000
The video is closely associated with Halloween, and
fans worldwide re-enact its zombie dance.

25
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
The Library of Congress described it as the most famous music video of all time, and it has
been named the greatest video by various publications and readers' polls.

26
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,000
In 2009, Michael Jackson's Thriller became the first music video inducted into the US National Film
Registry by the Library of Congress as "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

27
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,000
It reached one billion views on YouTube in 2024.

28
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:10,000
The film explores themes of dancing, date, narration, music video, zombie.

29
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:38,000
The tone is dark and intense.
